Pyxis builds unmodified conventional read/write sources as a static library.
Its public configuration is generated by upstream awk/preprocessor scripts,
with the simplified read/write API disabled. Architecture-specific acceleration,
shared libraries and upstream programs/tests are omitted. Standard stdio,
setjmp error recovery, floating-point and ancillary APIs remain enabled.

The archive consumes the separately exported zlib core and Pyxis libc; there
are no source patches, compatibility stubs or host-libc dependencies. Consumers
must use the matching pnglibconf.h installed beside png.h and pngconf.h.
